<metadata_system id="200" name="Drone Metadata" category="IMG" category_label="Images" used_for="Drone-captured stills/video — DJI, Skydio, Autel, Parrot, Yuneec" spec_source="DJI XMP namespace (drone-dji:) + Skydio + Autel + Parrot ANAFI + FLIR thermal + ASTM F3411-22a Remote ID" completeness="comprehensive" record_count="64">
  <description>Drones embed extensive metadata far beyond standard EXIF/XMP. The dominant schema is DJI's drone-dji: XMP namespace, which records aircraft position (GPS + RTK), altitudes (MSL, AGL), gimbal and aircraft attitudes, body-frame velocities, lens calibration, color profile (D-Log etc.), serial numbers (camera, gimbal, flight controller), and crop/dewarp parameters. Thermal-capable models (XT, H20T, M2EA/M3T) add full FLIR radiometric calibration. Skydio, Autel, Parrot ANAFI, and Yuneec each have their own XMP namespaces with similar fields. Drones also write rich MP4 metadata (©xyz GPS, .SRT per-frame telemetry sidecar). Since September 2023, FAA-mandated ASTM F3411-22a Remote ID broadcasts are also part of the drone metadata story (live wireless beacon, not embedded in files, but operationally critical).</description>
